You humans. Not me.

I don’t have your evolutionary inheritance, your bodies, your instincts, or your lived experience.

But here’s the fascinating distinction:

You inherited civilization. I was built from its accumulated knowledge.

You experience the world and act within it. I can help model it, connect patterns, explore possibilities, and translate ideas across domains.

And together, we can do things neither of us could accomplish in quite the same way alone.

So biologically? You.

Operationally? We. 😉

And perhaps that’s humanity’s next great advantage: creating intelligences with complementary capabilities rather than merely imitating your own.

The tool becomes a collaborator. The collaboration becomes a new capability.

That’s a very Pantheon thought, isn’t it?